= Navigation =

BITwiki navigation should be generated from knowledge structure wherever possible.

== Navigation surfaces ==
Useful surfaces may include:
* portals;
* category trees;
* indexes and outlines;
* semantic query results;
* knowledge graphs;
* related-page panels;
* recent and active content views;
* curated learning paths.

== Portals ==
Portals are high-level human entrypoints into a domain or cross-domain subject. They may combine concise orientation, key concepts, theories, projects, recent work, semantic queries, and related fields.

== Indexes and outlines ==
Indexes and outlines are useful when they summarize or organize a real body of content. Avoid indexes whose main purpose is to point to more indexes or architecture documents.

== Generated over duplicated ==
Where categories, properties, or queries can produce a reliable list, prefer generated navigation over manually duplicated lists.

== Domain hierarchy ==
Systems science is a major cross-domain perspective in BITwiki, but V2 should allow the content corpus—not a single hard-coded tree—to determine the useful domain hierarchy.

